The forgetting rate quantifies how much knowledge of old tasks has been lost after training on new tasks. As formalized in (10), F.Ra captures the maximum performance drop observed on each prior task between its peak and its final value. A higher F.Ra signals that learning new tasks erodes consolidated knowledge—precisely the failure mode that an effective continual learning algorithm should minimize.
